  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The H-index of an array is defined to be the maximum integer HHH such that there are at least HHH elements in the array which are greater than or equal to HHH.\n\nYou're given an integer array AAA and a positive integer KKK. You can do the following operation as many times as you want (possibly, none):\n\n\nPick two indices iii and jjj such that AiA_iAi​ is divisible KKK and AjA_jAj​ is not divisible by KKK; then divide AiA_iAi​ by KKK and multiply AjA_jAj​ by KKK.\nFind the maximum possible H-index of AAA that can be attained after performing the above operation as many times as you like.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the size of the array and the parameter KKK as described in the statement.\nThe next line contains NNN space separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum H-index you can achieve.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "2≤K≤1092 \\leq K \\leq 10^92≤K≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5 2\n3 5 4 1 10\n2 3\n9 1\n3 2\n2 16 2",
        "output": "4\n2\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choose i=5i = 5i=5 and j=1j = 1j=1, dividing A5A_5A5​ by K=2K = 2K=2 and multiplying A1A_1A1​ by 222.\nNow, the array becomes [6,5,4,1,5][6, 5, 4, 1, 5][6,5,4,1,5]. There are four elements ≥4\\geq 4≥4, so the H-index is 444.\nIt can be shown that this is optimal.\nTest case 222: Choose i=1i = 1i=1 and j=2j = 2j=2, turning AAA into [3,3][3, 3][3,3] which has H-index 222. This is optimal.\nTest case 333: We cannot do any operations to multiply A1A_1A1​ and A3A_3A3​ since they are already divisible by 222."
      }
    ]
  },
